mode: "100644"
text: "# The TEACH framework — teach one thing well, accurately, in the right format\n\nA content-angle layer that **feeds the format writers.** The agent **targets the lesson + ensures accuracy +\narranges it + routes it to the format + harvests saves**; the **format writers** build it; the **design/image\ntools** make the visuals; **WoopSocial publishes + serializes.**\n\n## T — Target one teachable thing\n- **One process / point / next-step.** **Flashcard, not chapter.** A **genuinely useful** topic **within real\n  expertise** — not a recycled generic tip. If it can't be taught well in one piece, **split into a series.**\n\n## E — Earn trust with accuracy\n- **Be correct.** **Cite sources** for stats/claims. **Stay within genuine expertise.** **YMYL** (health/\n  finance/legal/safety): add a **not-professional-advice disclaimer** + point to a pro. **Never fabricate steps\n  or stats.** *Teaching wrong info destroys authority.*\n\n## A — Arrange the lesson\n- **Hook/cover** (\"is this for me?\" + the payoff, specific, <8–10 words) → **context/problem** → **one step or\n  idea per unit** → **recap** → **specific CTA.** Pick a structure: **step-by-step / PAS / myth-bust / data.**\n  **8–12 units** (12–20 for deep guides); **every unit earns its place.**\n\n## C — Carry it to the right format\n- **Carousel** (reference/frameworks — the save king) → `carousel-writer` · **tutorial video** (process/demo) →\n  `reels-script`/`tiktok-script` · **thread** → `thread-writer` · **post** → `caption-writer`. The **cover\n  hook** → `hook-writer`; the **visual** → `design-and-templates`/the image tools. **CTA:** save / send to X /\n  **comment GUIDE** (→ `lead-magnets-and-funnels`).\n\n## H — Harvest saves + serialize\n- **Saves/sends = the top authority signal** (measure those, not likes). **Serialize** into a recognizable\n  weekly series (`content-calendar`); **evergreen** → repurpose one lesson across formats\n  (`content-recycling`). **WoopSocial publishes + schedules the series.**\n\n## The lesson brief a request should fill\n```\nTOPIC: one teachable thing (process/point/next-step) -- within real expertise; useful, not generic\nACCURACY: sources for any stat/claim; within-expertise? YMYL -> disclaimer + point to a pro; nothing fabricated\nLESSON: hook/cover (is-this-for-me + payoff) -> context/problem -> one step per unit -> recap -> CTA  | structure: step/PAS/myth/data | 8-12 units\nFORMAT: carousel (carousel-writer) / video (reels-script) / thread (thread-writer) / post (caption-writer); cover -> hook-writer; visual -> design tools\nCTA: save this / send to the person who handles X / comment GUIDE (-> lead-magnets). SERIALIZE: series in content-calendar. METRIC: saves/sends.\n```\n"
